{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys","id":1103046,"title":"Finding Keys","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T02:21:41-07:00","id":1103046,"title":"Finding Keys","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Throughout the course of the chronicle, every time the<br /> character gains a Beat in a scene involving angels, demons,<br /> stigmatics, or the God-Machine, the player makes a reflexive<br /> Intelligence + Wits roll. If she is following her Agenda at the<br /> time (and the player makes a convincing case for this to the<br /> Storyteller), the player can add her Primum to the roll. </div> </div> </div>Am I missing something, or in the default format of the game (where the players are all demons) doesn't this basically mean that anytime you get a beat you get to roll to figure out your next key, since you're presumably with the other players? <br /> <br /> That seems...dumb. This would lead to a player fully filling out their Cipher and hitting Primum 4 within 6 sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T03:11:57-07:00","id":1103059,"title":"","content":"Depends on the game. You could start out slow, building the &quot;mortal&quot; lives of the Demon(s) before dropping G-M plots on them. And resolving Conditions like Guilty or Addicted don't necessarily involve the G-M. And I would count if any of the above are nearby, if they aren't\u200b involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T03:39:01-07:00","id":1103069,"title":"","content":"When I've run and played Demon with my group, &quot;a scene involving demons&quot; implies NPCs <i>qua </i>demons. Or maybe some question or task specific to the demonic condition. It's not just &quot;any scene with the PCs in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Slightly aside from that, my players were vocally really happy with the idea of getting Primum 4 and completing the Cipher after just two or three stories. Fast early advancement isn't necessarily a negative, especially if the game isn't expected to run that long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T04:05:56-07:00","id":1103073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys?p=1103069#post1103069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I've run and played Demon with my group, &quot;a scene involving demons&quot; implies NPCs <i>qua </i>demons. Or maybe some question or task specific to the demonic condition. It's not just &quot;any scene with the PCs in it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm going to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys?p=1103069#post1103069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly aside from that, my players were vocally really happy with the idea of getting Primum 4 and completing the Cipher after just two or three stories. Fast early advancement isn't necessarily a negative, especially if the game isn't expected to run that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree, but six sessions is a little <i>too</i> fast, even by my tastes. Especially since my current campaign is going to last for at least 60 or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:04:38-07:00","id":1103154,"title":"","content":"Should be easy to tweak it a bit so that either the rolls happen slower or at specific points or with penalties that lesson as time goes on. I see no reason why it wouldn't be too hard to tweak it for your setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:53:38-07:00","id":1103208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys#post1103046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something, or in the default format of the game (where the players are all demons) doesn't this basically mean that anytime you get a beat you get to roll to figure out your next key, since you're presumably with the other players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Espionage means the default game assumes demon characters need to navigate the difficulties of Cover management to meet without drawing too much suspicious and will endeavor to maintain a certain degree of plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> If you only ever run scenes involving Unchained Business in a game that actively rewards you for getting through sessions and stories without breaking false identity that disguises your demonic nature, then yes, you'll absolutely end up racing through the bonus Primum. That's no more &quot;dumb&quot; than the PCs rapidly accruing magical power through Arcane Experience in a Mage game that spends all of its time on the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The solution is to put actual weight on the mundane side of the setting as it relates to the characters if you don't want them diving wholesale into the supernatural end of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:00:49-07:00","id":1103213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys?p=1103208#post1103208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Espionage means the default game assumes demon characters need to navigate the difficulties of Cover management to meet without drawing too much suspicious and will endeavor to maintain a certain degree of plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> If you only ever run scenes involving Unchained Business in a game that actively rewards you for getting through sessions and stories without breaking false identity that disguises your demonic nature, then yes, you'll absolutely end up racing through the bonus Primum. That's no more &quot;dumb&quot; than the PCs rapidly accruing magical power through Arcane Experience in a Mage game that spends all of its time on the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The solution is to put actual weight on the mundane side of the setting as it relates to the characters if you don't want them diving wholesale into the supernatural end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this is irrelevant. A scene still 'involves demons' even if all of the demons are in Cover and acting totally mundane. If I have an Aspiration to crack open a cold one with the boys, and we all roll down to the bar and grab a drink, and I get a beat, if 'the boys' are demons, I get closer to finding my keys per RAW.<br /> <br /> Yes, that <b>is</b> dumb.<br /> <br /> Before you address the absurdity of the situation, please note that I specifically called out the most absurd situation I could think of that would still apply under RAW.<br /> <br /> That's obviously not RAI, and I've already decided how to address that - Caladriu's method works best for my games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:49:30-07:00","id":1103227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys?p=1103213#post1103213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this is irrelevant. A scene still 'involves demons' even if all of the demons are in Cover and acting totally mundane. If I have an Aspiration to crack open a cold one with the boys, and we all roll down to the bar and grab a drink, and I get a beat, if 'the boys' are demons, I get closer to finding my keys per RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Crack open a cold one with Mr. Molotov and the crew&quot; is well within spec for Tempters and other socially-oriented demons and moving the game to the point where your characters have made a coordinated meeting as demons as a meaningful story beat is perfectly fine for justifying a <i>roll to get a hint</i>.<br /> <br /> You can accomplish the same thing with an Aspiration of &quot;Avoid angelic detection&quot; after a local demon draws down a manhunt by not breaking character when the hunters go door-to-door asking after suspicious individuals. You can accomplish the same thing by having an Aspiration to bond with your Offspring. It's an aggregation mechanism for Things Of The Machine, not a means of solely encouraging overt risk over the lower-key risk of keeping close to the Demiurge's works.<br /> <br /> The Cipher is mechanically completely incidental to most aspects of the game's subtlety-oriented half. It's one of the tempting aspects of the loud side of the game, but you can go through a whole game without pursuing it. If you want to discourage Cipher hints stemming from the quieter and less overtly supernatural means of Beat acquisition that can prompt the roll, the fact that it's a roll means you have penalties at your disposal, or flatly reducing the roll to one Attribute.<br /> <br /> It's a character self-discovery mechanic that requires you to spend Experiences on supernatural powers to make proper use of and if you've bought more than one extra dot of Primum then completion promises to nudge the character into the superhuman-drawbacks segment of the chart. Characters that take a more measured approach will see more narrative slack freed up from not rushing the investigation process and characters that jump right in will have to balance a more concrete goal with less resources on every other front.<br /> <br /> I didn't say the prospect of gaming Aspirations to this end <i>wasn't</i> dumb, I said it was <i>no more</i> dumb than a hypothetical game of Mage where you maintain an Obsession of &quot;find seven new Mysteries in a week&quot; and then spend the whole story poking around the Realms Invisible to rack up Mana and Arcane Experience. You know what you're going to do to resolve this problem that occurs from a technical reading of a mechanic in a particular playstyle that doesn't lean heavily on most of the genre-widgets to maintain pressure on the PCs. There's no need to state the obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T12:12:10-07:00","id":1103231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no need to state the obvious. </div> </div> </div>I had a hell of a lot written about this, but it's better if I don't post it.<br /> Thank you for your contribution. You made fair points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T19:16:34-07:00","id":1103359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1103046-finding-keys#post1103046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems...dumb. This would lead to a player fully filling out their Cipher and hitting Primum 4 within 6 sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is basically exactly how I found things went in my own Demon game. Two players had unlocked their Ciphers completely after five sessions. All bar one of the five players had done so after nine. Worked really well for a short nine session campaign like that, it felt very well paced, though I can see the concern in a longer game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}